  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/common-microsyntaxes.html#rules-for-parsing-floating-point-number-values\r\n\r\n>15. <i>Conversion</i>: Let <var>S</var> be the set of finite IEEE 754 double-precision floating-point values except −0, but with two special values added: 2<sup>1024</sup> and −2<sup>1024</sup>.\r\n>16. Let <var>rounded-value</var> be the number in <var>S</var> that is closest to\r\n   <var>value</var>, selecting the number with an even significand if there are two equally close values. (The two special values 2<sup>1024</sup> and −2<sup>1024</sup> are considered to have even significands for this purpose.)\r\n>17. If <var>rounded-value</var> is 2<sup>1024</sup> or −2<sup>1024</sup>, return an error.\r\n\r\nBut −2<sup>1024</sup> = 2<sup>1024</sup>, because the power exponent is an even number.\r\n\r\n\"−2<sup>1024</sup>\" should be write \"−(2<sup>1024</sup>)\" or \"2<sup>1024</sup> * -1\" for more accurately.",
